      "text": "Robert Hill showed in 1937 that isolated chloroplasts evolve oxygen in light when given an artificial electron acceptor.",
      "label": "p6",
      "factual": true,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "a6",
      "text": "Robert Hill first described the Hill reaction in 1952.",
      "label": "p7",
      "factual": false,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "a7",
      "text": "Oxygen evolution in the Hill reaction proceeded without any reduction of carbon dioxide.",
